{"lesson":{"title":"Defence Can Change Before You Hit","hook":"A wide ball does not decide your answer on its own. Your arrival can change the options.","readinessLesson":true,"memHTML":"<span>Need time? Buy it with height and depth.</span>","tomorrow":"When pulled wide, check how much time you need to recover. If you arrive early and see a real opening, a controlled change of direction may be available.","cue":"Need time? Buy it with height and depth.","pro":{"player":"Carlos Alcaraz","label":"Alcaraz · Buy time to change the point","moment":"The spectacular counterattack is the part we remember. In his Winning on Defense overview, strategist Craig O’Shannessy includes Alcaraz among the players he analyses and highlights changes of speed, spin and height as ways to escape defence. There is more than one reply to being pushed wide.","read":"Your next point: choose the time you need. Still stretched? Height and depth can give you time to recover. Arrived with control and a real opening? Reassess the pressure shot. Defend the situation you are in, not the one you were in a moment ago.","src":"Craig O’Shannessy · Winning on Defense · public overview","url":"https://braingametennis.com/webinar-73-winning-on-defense/"},"callbackTags":["movement_read","time_space_balance"],"finaleScene":"ed3","finaleFull":true,"steps":[{"ph":"Read the point","short":"Read","name":"Choose your plan","scene":"ed1","reveal":true,"noTargets":true,"sit":"Their ball takes you towards the sideline. Watch both players.","q":"Which plan fits this point?","opts":["Drive down the line, with margin","High and deep crosscourt, then recover"],"correct":1,"payoff":"Still travelling out? Give yourself time to get back.","principle":"Read your arrival as well as the ball and the opponent.","why":"The line is open, but you are still travelling to the ball. A higher, deeper crosscourt reply gives you more margin and flight time for recovery. It does not guarantee that they cannot attack.","cues":null,"rail":["Watch the point","Choose your plan","Then inspect"],"unlock":"Read the whole situation","take":"Still travelling out? Give yourself time to get back.","lines":{"A":"An opening alone does not make the change of direction easy.","B":"The extra flight time can help you recover."}},{"ph":"Read the point","short":"Read","name":"Choose your plan","scene":"ed2","reveal":true,"noTargets":true,"sit":"The same ball and opponent. Watch your arrival this time.","q":"Which plan fits this point?","opts":["Drive down the line, with margin","High and deep crosscourt, then recover"],"correct":0,"payoff":"Earlier arrival can open a choice; it does not require an attack.","principle":"Read your arrival as well as the ball and the opponent.","why":"You have reached the preparation position sooner and they are still across the court. The line can apply pressure with margin. High and deep is also a sound choice; the useful change is that you now have an option.","cues":null,"rail":["Watch the point","Choose your plan","Then inspect"],"unlock":"Read the whole situation","take":"Earlier arrival can open a choice; it does not require an attack.","lines":{"A":"Earlier arrival makes the open line a reasonable pressure shot.","B":"Also sound: keep the margin and recover."},"compareArrival":"ed1","alsoOk":[1]},{"ph":"Read the point","short":"Read","name":"Choose your plan","scene":"ed3","reveal":true,"noTargets":true,"sit":"Another rally. Choose your plan.","q":"Which plan fits this point?","opts":["High and deep crosscourt, then recover","Drive down the line, with margin"],"correct":0,"payoff":"Other wing, same question: how much time do you need?","principle":"Read your arrival as well as the ball and the opponent.","why":"You are still moving wide on the backhand side. The opponent is central. Choose height and depth to help your recovery instead of treating the sideline as an invitation to redirect.","cues":null,"rail":["Watch the point","Choose your plan","Then inspect"],"unlock":"Read 